				{"name":"Beat This!","short":"beatth(1)","start":"2026-08-22 01:05","end":"2026-08-22 01:55"},
				{"name":"Green Man Pop Quiz","short":"greenm1(1)","start":"2026-08-22 12:00","end":"2026-08-22 13:30"},
				{"name":"Zack Polanski in conversation w/Will Hayward","short":"zackpo(1)","start":"2026-08-22 13:45","end":"2026-08-22 14:30","type":"other","blurb":"Leader of the Green Party of England and Wales, Zack Polanski sits down with journalist Will Hayward to talk about challenges and hope. The only thing everyone agrees with at the moment is that what we have right now isn’t working. The Green leader has shot to prominence in recent years with an unapologetic and forthright form of green politics. Investigative journalist, author and Guardian columnist Will Hayward is widely considered one of the leading voices covering Wales and Welsh politics. Together they discuss what the future could be, why people should hope and how we keep the lights on in a world determined to get darker."},
				{"name":"Neil Collins in conversation with Teresa Delfino","short":"neilco(1)","start":"2026-08-22 14:45","end":"2026-08-22 15:30","type":"other","artist":"How Wales Conquered the '90s Charts: Neil Collins in conversation with Teresa Delfino","blurb":"“Every day when I wake up, I thank the Lord I’m Welsh…” If the story of Wales in the ‘90s was a movie plot, it would all seem so far-fetched. Thankfully, it was all true. Featuring fresh analysis and new interviews, International Velvet: How Wales Conquered the '90s Charts revisits the unforgettable 'Cool Cymru' era when Manic Street Preachers, Catatonia, Super Furry Animals, Stereophonics, Gorky’s Zygotic Mynci, Feeder, 60ft Dolls and many more won over the masses. Author and journalist Neil Collins is joined in conversation with journalist Teresa Delfino."},
				{"name":"Steve Mason (The Beta Band) in conversation w/Huw Stephens","short":"stevem(1)","start":"2026-08-22 15:45","end":"2026-08-22 16:30","type":"other","blurb":"Scottish singer-songwriter and founding member of The Beta Band, Steve Mason has long been at the centre of tales of unruly non-conformism and destructive self-sabotage. Now in his long-awaited autobiography he sets the record straight (well, straight-ish) with his wildly funny, brilliantly told memoir of youth culture, failure, success, sadness and redemption. Steve Mason is joined in conversation with broadcaster Huw Stephens."},
				{"name":"Elizabeth Alker in conversation with Huw Stephens","short":"elizab(1)","start":"2026-08-22 16:45","end":"2026-08-22 17:30","type":"other","artist":"Everything We Do Is Music","blurb":"The worlds of pop and rock owe a much greater debt to the classical canon than we realise. A direct and fascinating lineage draws from the experimentalism of Pierre Henry to The Beatles’ Tomorrow Never Knows, from Stockhausen to Donna Summer’s I Feel Love. In Everything We Do is Music, Elizabeth Alker shines a light on the fertile ground that exists between the borders of classical music and pop. Elizabeth Alker will be in conversation with broadcaster Huw Stephens."},
				{"name":"Kevin Rowland in conversation w/ Sophie Williams","short":"kevinr(1)","start":"2026-08-22 17:45","end":"2026-08-22 18:30","type":"other","artist":"Bless Me Father","blurb":"In his astonishing and subversive memoir, Bless Me Father, Kevin Rowland lays bare his unvarnished life story for the very first time. From the juvenile courts of his troubled teenage years to the early days of the New Romantic scene in the late ’70s and beyond, he recounts his darkest hours, deepest desires and greatest joys. Back with a new album as Dexys Midnight Runners, Kevin Rowland is joined in conversation with journalist and broadcaster Sophie Williams."},
