				{"name":"Samantha Morton's Honest Playlist with the Guardian","short":"samant(1)","start":"2026-08-23 12:00","end":"2026-08-23 13:00","type":"other","blurb":"The Guardian LIVE is joined by the iconic Samantha Morton. In a highly decorated career, Morton has won a Golden Globe Award, and has been nominated for three BAFTAs, eight BIFAs, an Emmy Award, and two Independent Spirit Awards. She was awarded the Richard Harris award at the 2023 BIFAs in recognition of her long career in support of independent film, and in 2024, she was the recipient of the BAFTA Fellowship, the highest honour bestowed by the British film industry, for career achievement.\n\nShe'll be in conversation with Kate Hutchinson as they chat about Morton's life through music and an Honest Playlist."},
				{"name":"Weird Walk hosts Stewart Lee in conversation w/ Tim Plester: a live podcast recording","short":"weirdw(1)","start":"2026-08-23 13:15","end":"2026-08-23 14:00","type":"other","blurb":"For this live Weird Walk podcast recording, Tim Plester - co-director of The Archivist, the new documentary about folklorist Doc Rowe - talks with renowned comedian Stewart Lee about folklore, hauntology, comedy, music and the ritual year. In the spirit of Weird Walk’s explorations of the histories and mysteries of the British landscape, expect digressions into ancient sites, countercultural memory and the strange pull of place."},
				{"name":"Kiri Pritchard-Mclean in conversation w/Tony Bontana & Henry Widdicombe","short":"kiripr(1)","start":"2026-08-23 14:15","end":"2026-08-23 15:15","type":"other","artist":"Making Art From the Tough Stuff","blurb":"Welsh comedian and broadcaster Kiri Pritchard-McLean hosts a panel with guests - writer and comedian Henry Widdicombe and rapper Tony Bontana - about making work that reflects and processes painful life events. Come along for this illuminating chat from three artists who have chosen to cast a spotlight on their own darkest hours."},
				{"name":"Richard Russell of XL Records in conversation with Eamonn Forde","short":"richar1(1)","start":"2026-08-23 15:15","end":"2026-08-23 16:00","type":"other","blurb":"Ahead of his performance as Everything is Recorded, join Richard Russell for an illuminating conversation about his remarkable life in music. For almost 30 years as label boss, producer, and talent conductor at XL Recordings, Richard has discovered, shaped and nurtured the artists who have rewritten the musical dictionary of the 21st century, including The Prodigy, The White Stripes, Adele, M.I.A, Dizzee Rascal and Giggs. His acclaimed memoir Liberation Through Hearing tells the remarkable story of XL Recordings' three decades on the frontline of innovation in music. Richard is in conversation with journalist Eamonn Forde."},
				{"name":"Folding Rock Magazine Presents Anthony Shapland w/Robert Harries","short":"foldin(1)","start":"2026-08-23 16:15","end":"2026-08-23 17:00","type":"other","blurb":"Hailed by The Observer as ‘one of the best debut novels in years’, Anthony Shapland’s A Room Above a Shop already feels destined to become a British literary classic. The writer and artist joins Folding Rock editor and co-founder Robert Harries to discuss his poignant story of queer love set against the turbulent backdrop of Section 28, the age-of-consent debate, and the devastating HIV and AIDS crisis."},
				{"name":"Maisie Williams & Lowri Roberts in conversation w/Teresa Delfino","short":"maisie(1)","start":"2026-08-23 17:15","end":"2026-08-23 18:00","type":"other","blurb":"Emmy-nominated actress, Maisie Williams and long-time collaborator Lowri Roberts invite you to an honest conversation about activism, creativity, and criticism in a world where everything we do is posted online. Drawing on their efforts to drive positive environmental change, they confront the messy reality of trying to do good in an imperfect world. This talk encourages action over perfection celebrating the power of ‘just having a go’. With thanks to Media Cymru."},
